<title>AUSTRIA: Erste says prelim 96 op profit up 11 pct.</title>
<headline>Erste says prelim 96 op profit up 11 pct.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian savings bank Die Erste Oesterreichische Sparkasse-Bank (First Austrian) said on Tuesday preliminary 1996 operating profit rose 11 percent and expected net profit to improve more than 10 percent from 1995.</p>
<p>The company said it expected to be able to at least match last year's dividend payment of 16 schillings this year as well.</p>
<p>Die Erste said preliminary operating profit reached 1.95 billion schillings, up from 1.76 billion last year. In 1995, the savings bank chalked up a net profit of 491 million schillings.</p>
<p>Die Erste is a member of a consortium headed by insurer EA-Generali which is bidding to buy the state's stake in Creditanstalt-Bankverein. -- Vienna newsroom, +431 531 12253</p>
</text>
